criteria.note:
All six items sit above the bar at 360x640:
- the worn hero, 77-386;
- the H1 (Cormorant 27, title case), 398-426;
- the price row: ₹2,399, the strike, incl. GST and 'Arrives gift-boxed';
- the ruled ladder, 470-538;
- 'Free insured delivery, est. 18-20 Nov · COD available', ending at 562;
- the bar from 575 (measure.json).
No line wraps. The ladder is now a typographic table, not a coupon box, which is the right idiom.

Remaining art faults:
- The price (Cormorant 23) and the three ladder figures (Cormorant 19, ink) differ by only 1.21x, so the eye meets four near-equal rupee figures in 90px. With the strike and the button that makes six on one screen.
- 'Any pieces · taken off in your bag, no code' reads as a fragment.
- The piece sits low in the hero (see C2).

The rail is strong:
- a vertical list with the ring first as the rhodium match;
- full names, a metal line from FACTS and 'Only 3 left' in ink-2 from stock;
- 88x44 Adds that toggle to an ink '✓ In bag' (set_after.png);
- deep-sage marginal lines in rupees;
- an outlined 'Add all four · ₹3,987'.

Art faults:
- The ring's metal line wraps and orphans '5-9' on a line of its own (full.png y 1750-1820).
- The sub-line 'Any second piece takes 10% off your whole bag, a third 20%, a fourth 30%.' and the empty-bag summary 'The bracelet alone ₹2,399 / Any second piece takes 10% off your whole bag.' are the second and third tellings of the ladder within two screens. The summary is also a deep-ivory box that is not a bag.
- The three thumbnails sit on three grounds (terracotta, cream plinth, grey). That needs the matched set shoot (roadmap).

The 10-today set is met:
- an honest 3.3 s cut that loads only on tap;
- a mehendi-wrist poster;
- 'Creator collaboration · Riya' on the slide, with the sub-line 'Riya, a creator we collaborated with, styling it with mehendi.' (screens_2.jpg panel 1);
- the second tile shown as a still with no fake play button.

Art faults:
- At 9:16 the second tile shows a ceiling fan, a bare ceiling and wall frames above Riya (full.png y 2850-2950). It is the cheapest-looking detail on the page.
- The label 'Creator collaboration · Riya' appears four times in two screens, so the captions carry no information about their frames.

Scored for type and legibility. Taps and contrast belong to UX:
- every target is at least 44px and the text floor is 11px;
- ink-2 at 0.72 on ivory passes.

The type system is still not a system. m1.js counts 34 distinct text styles on the visible page (family, size, weight, case, tracking, colour), against the 8 asked for in round 1:
- Cormorant runs at 12 sizes: 13, 15, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 23, 24, 25 and 27;
- Jost has half-pixel sizes: 12.5 for .ship and .row .eff, 13.5 for .lad2 and .dr-lad;
- the '₹1,709' in 'All four · you save' is Cormorant at 13px, a spindly hairline serif;
- set names ask for Cormorant 400, which is not loaded (L169), so the browser picks the 500 face anyway.

Restraint is now real:
- two families only (measure.json);
- palette: ivory, ivory-deep, ink and deep sage; no new hex except #fff in the UPI discs;
- radius 0 except the bag's 10px checkout;
- no badges or stars;
- one ink primary;
- a deep-sage footer and a 48px section rhythm.
This now sits closer to Mejuri than to any Indian bench fold (r2art/bench_r2.jpg).

One fix made things worse. 'Up close' became a single image, as asked, but .bleed renders 360x792, not square (m1.js). The width=720 height=792 attributes set height: 792px, which defeats aspect-ratio: 1/1, and object-fit: cover then shows the macro's out-of-focus top. The result is about 1.2 screens of blank beige blur before a stone appears (screens_1.jpg panel 3 lower half; full.png y 1673-2100). It is the largest visual fault on the page.

Smaller issues:
- The two 48px outlined Reviews boxes are the heaviest objects on their screen, and they give an empty state the weight of a primary action.
- The UPI marks are three overlapping white discs with 1px ink rings and border-radius 50% (L138). They read as an avatar stack, and they carry the only saturated colour on the first screen.

fixes.change:
Two changes on the Riya slide.

1. Move the plate:
- Set `.sl .play { left: 10px; bottom: 10px; top: auto; transform: none; }`, the same corner as the hero chip.
- Keep the 'Creator collaboration · Riya' tag at top-left.

2. Reorder the gallery to worn, macro, plaster, velvet, Riya, size, box:
- SLIDES = ['worn','macro','plaster','velvet','riya','size','box'];
- ASSET: p2/velvet → 3; riya/reel/creator → 4;
- in the head script, `if (t === 'riya' || t === 'reel') m.slide = 4`;
- the counter and aria label follow the DOM order.

Replace the bitmap with an inline SVG ruler at the slide's width (viewBox 0 0 320 72, width 100%, max 320px):
- a 1px ink baseline from 0 to 24 cm, with ticks every cm (5px; 9px at 0, 5, 10, 15 and 20);
- numerals 0, 5, 10, 15, 20, 24 cm in Jost 11px ink-2;
- the bracelet as a 2px ink line from 0 to 18, with '18 cm' in Jost 11px 500 above its end;
- the wrist range as a 6px band in deep sage at 40% from 15 to 19, labelled 'fits wrists 15–19 cm' in Jost 11px deep sage.

Keep the figcaption text exactly. Drop size-band.jpg (12 KB, one request).
